# Diabetic Retinopathy Screening App

Streamlit app that grades a retinal fundus image on the 5-stage DR scale
(No DR / Mild / Moderate / Severe / Proliferative) and shows a headline
**Referable DR: Yes/No** badge.

Model weights (`best_qwk_final.pth`, EfficientNet-B4) are **not** stored in
this repo — the app downloads them automatically from Google Drive on first
run (see `GDRIVE_FILE_ID` in `app.py`).

## Run locally

```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd <your-repo>
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
```

First run will download the model weights (~70-80MB) automatically; later
runs use the cached local copy.

## Deploy

Works as-is on:
- **Streamlit Community Cloud** — connect the repo, set `app.py` as the entrypoint, deploy.
- **Hugging Face Spaces** (Streamlit SDK) — push this repo, no secrets needed since the Drive file is public link-shared.
- Any VM/container — just `pip install -r requirements.txt && streamlit run app.py`.

## Updating the model

If you retrain and get a new `best_qwk_final.pth`:
1. Upload the new file to Google Drive, share as "Anyone with the link".
2. Copy its file ID (the part between `/d/` and `/view` in the share link).
3. Replace `GDRIVE_FILE_ID` in `app.py` with the new ID.
4. Delete any old cached `best_qwk_final.pth` on the deployment so it re-downloads.

## Disclaimer

This is a research/screening-support tool, not a certified diagnostic device.
